      "answer": "TL;DR: The **Council Chambers** actively interfere via **activated runes/wards, illusory walls, and environmental chaos (lighting, space, reinforcements)**\u2014it\u2019s a magically trapped, perception-warping battlefield.\n\nKey Attributes  \n- Defenses (OBSERVED): **Runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell**, plus **ancient defensive wards** that affect the battle environment. These can trigger effects like the arcane trap bursts already impacting the Players (paralysis, force damage).  \n- Defenses (OBSERVED): **Illusory Walls** present in parts of the room, contributing to disorientation and mispositioning mid-fight.  \n- Geography (OBSERVED): **Large circular room with a central table and high, arched ceilings**\u2014verticality and line-of-sight issues (e.g., hard to reach elevated targets). Also includes a **hidden trapdoor**, which can introduce threats or movement complications.  \n- Atmosphere (OBSERVED): **Almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**, creating chaotic visibility and possibly obscuring hazards.  \n- Current Activity (CANON/OBSERVED blend): **Guards are being drawn here as reinforcements**, adding pressure over time.  \n\nNet effect: shifting terrain (illusions), reactive magic (runes/wards), and escalating pressure (reinforcements + chaotic visibility) all stack to disrupt positioning, targeting, and planning.",
