      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12\u2014specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014and there\u2019s no evidence his corruption was cured before death.\n\nThe **OBSERVED physical_condition** explicitly includes **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, which is a terminal outcome and overrides earlier states like being invisible or escaping. Supporting this, **ent_bonogo** is noted to have \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d confirming the kill occurred in play.\n\nRegarding corruption: the Wolf previously had **\u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), indicating active corruption. There is no OBSERVED fact stating this condition was removed or resolved prior to death, so the most grounded conclusion is that he died **while still corrupted**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, previously had oily sheen in eyes (corrupted)\n- Operational Status: Previously escaping/invisible, but superseded by death\n- Faction/Role: Cultist, central adversary\n- History: Attacked by Bonogo; ultimately killed and beheaded by him",
