      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur using illusions and escape tactics; after, he\u2019s a broken, desperate figure who ends up **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** with clear signs of corruption and regret.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is operating as a **cultist saboteur** and **second-in-command of the guard**.\n- He actively **manipulates the council** (Deception, misdirection) and **orders attacks** (e.g., directing Thalia).\n- In combat, he\u2019s evasive and tricky: uses **illusory duplicates**, **Invisibility**, and attempts to **escape via a secret tunnel**.\n- Mentally, he\u2019s alert and calculating, though already showing strain (\u201csensed danger\u201d).\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state shifts dramatically to **desperate and remorseful**: \u201cbegging for someone to release him,\u201d \u201cbegging to be killed,\u201d and \u201cfeels regret.\u201d\n- Physically, he shows heavy corruption: **\u201coily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**\n- His arc ends definitively with **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur \u2192 defeated target\n- Tactics: Illusions/invisibility \u2192 none (post-defeat)\n- Mental State: Calculated \u2192 desperate, regretful\n- Physical Condition: Mobile, evasive \u2192 corrupted, then **decapitated**\n- Allegiance: Cult-linked throughout, but more visibly corrupted by the end",
      "embedding_similarity": null
